> \(i\) Evidence of insurance policies and endorsements in form, scope, and substance satisfactory to the Administrative Agent, including lender\'s loss payable and additional insured endorsements in favor of the Administrative Agent;
>
> \(j\) Delivery of customary legal opinions from the Borrower\'s counsel, Hargrove, Pennington & Locke LLP, covering such matters as corporate authority, enforceability, no conflicts, and other customary matters;
>
> \(k\) Delivery of lien search results (UCC, federal and state tax lien, and judgment lien searches) in all relevant jurisdictions, confirming no prior liens on the Collateral other than Permitted Liens;
>
> \(l\) Payment of all fees and expenses due and payable on the Closing Date, including fees under the Fee Letter, reasonable and documented legal fees and expenses of Caldwell Strauss & Moran LLP (as Lender\'s counsel), and all other closing costs;
>
> \(m\) Receipt of all \"know your customer\" (KYC) and anti-money laundering (AML) documentation for the Borrower, each Guarantor, and their respective beneficial owners, as required by applicable law and the internal policies of each Lender; and
>
> \(n\) Satisfaction of customary \"SunGard\" or \"certain funds\" limited conditionality provisions, pursuant to which certain representations, covenants, and default conditions shall be limited to Specified Representations and Specified Defaults (as such terms will be defined in the definitive Credit Agreement), consistent with market practice for acquisition financings of this type.
**[Section 7 --- Representations and Warranties]**
The definitive Credit Agreement shall contain representations and warranties customary for transactions of this type, including, without limitation, the following:
> \(a\) Corporate organization, existence, good standing, and qualification to do business in all jurisdictions where the ownership of its properties or the conduct of its business requires such qualification;
>
> \(b\) Due authorization, execution, delivery, and enforceability of the Credit Agreement and each other loan document;
>
> \(c\) No conflict with organizational documents, material agreements, or applicable law;
>
> \(d\) Financial statements --- the historical financial statements of the Borrower delivered to the Lenders fairly present in all material respects the financial condition and results of operations of the Borrower and its subsidiaries as of the dates and for the periods covered thereby, and have been prepared in accordance with GAAP consistently applied (subject to the absence of footnotes and year-end audit adjustments in the case of interim financial statements);
>
> \(e\) No Material Adverse Effect --- since December 31, 2024, there has been no event, circumstance, change, development, or condition that, individually or in the aggregate, has had or could reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect. The term \"Material Adverse Effect\" shall be defined in the definitive Credit Agreement in a manner consistent with customary MAE definitions for transactions of this type;
>
> \(f\) Litigation --- no action, suit, proceeding, or investigation is pending or, to the knowledge of the Borrower, threatened against the Borrower or any of its subsidiaries that could reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect;
>
> \(g\) Compliance with all applicable laws, rules, and regulations (including, without limitation, environmental laws and regulations, given the nature of the Borrower\'s business);
>
> \(h\) Tax matters --- all material tax returns have been timely filed and all material taxes have been paid, except as being contested in good faith with adequate reserves;
>
> \(i\) ERISA compliance --- no ERISA Event has occurred or is reasonably expected to occur that could reasonably be expected to have a Material Adverse Effect;
>
> \(j\) Accuracy of information --- all information provided by or on behalf of the Borrower and its subsidiaries to the Administrative Agent and the Lenders is accurate and complete in all material respects (and no such information contains any untrue statement of a material fact or omits a material fact necessary to make the statements therein, in the light of the circumstances under which they were made, not misleading);
>
> \(k\) Intellectual property --- the Borrower and its subsidiaries own or have valid rights to use all intellectual property necessary for the conduct of their business as currently conducted;
>
> \(l\) Insurance --- the Borrower and its subsidiaries maintain insurance coverages in such amounts and against such risks as are customary for companies of similar size in similar industries;
>
> \(m\) Solvency --- the Borrower and its subsidiaries, on a consolidated basis, are Solvent (as defined in the Credit Agreement) after giving pro forma effect to the Transactions;
>
> \(n\) Ownership of properties and assets; no liens other than Permitted Liens;
>
> \(o\) Use of proceeds in compliance with the terms of the Credit Agreement;
>
> \(p\) Federal Reserve margin regulations --- the Borrower is not engaged, principally or as one of its important activities, in the business of purchasing or carrying margin stock;
>
> \(q\) OFAC, anti-corruption, and anti-money laundering compliance;
>
> \(r\) Labor matters --- no strikes, lockouts, or material labor disputes; and
>
> \(s\) Environmental matters --- enhanced environmental representations appropriate for an environmental remediation and waste management services company, including compliance with all Environmental Laws, absence of material environmental liabilities, and no pending or threatened material environmental claims.
**[Section 8 --- Affirmative Covenants]**
The definitive Credit Agreement shall contain affirmative covenants customary for transactions of this type, including, without limitation, the following:
**Financial Reporting:**
> \(a\) *Annual Audited Financial Statements:* Within 120 days after the end of each fiscal year of the Borrower, audited consolidated financial statements of the Borrower and its subsidiaries for such fiscal year, audited by Stonebridge Thornton LLP or another independent registered public accounting firm of recognized national standing reasonably acceptable to the Administrative Agent, accompanied by an unqualified opinion thereon (or an opinion qualified only as to a going-concern qualification arising solely in connection with the approaching maturity of the Credit Facilities in the final year of the Term Loan maturity). Such financial statements shall include a consolidated balance sheet, consolidated statements of income, cash flows, and stockholders\' equity, and related notes, all prepared in accordance with GAAP consistently applied. For the avoidance of doubt, the annual audited financial statements shall be delivered within one hundred twenty (120) days of fiscal year end.
>
> \(b\) *Quarterly Unaudited Financial Statements:* Within 45 days after the end of each of the first three fiscal quarters of each fiscal year, unaudited consolidated financial statements of the Borrower and its subsidiaries, including a consolidated balance sheet, consolidated statements of income and cash flows, and such other financial information as the Administrative Agent may reasonably request, certified by a Responsible Officer as fairly presenting in all material respects the financial condition of the Borrower (subject to the absence of footnotes and normal year-end audit adjustments).
>
> \(c\) *Monthly Management Reporting:* Within 30 days after the end of each calendar month, monthly management reports in form and substance reasonably satisfactory to the Administrative Agent, including a summary income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow information. Monthly management reporting shall be required only during the first 12 months following the Closing Date; thereafter, monthly reporting shall be at the reasonable request of the Administrative Agent.
>
> \(d\) *Annual Budget and Financial Projections:* Within 45 days after the start of each fiscal year, an annual operating budget and financial projections for such fiscal year (including quarterly breakdowns), prepared in good faith and based on reasonable assumptions, in form and substance reasonably satisfactory to the Administrative Agent.
>
> \(e\) *Compliance Certificate:* Delivered concurrently with each set of annual and quarterly financial statements, a Compliance Certificate signed by a Responsible Officer of the Borrower, in the form attached to the Credit Agreement, certifying (i) compliance or non-compliance with each financial covenant set forth in Section 11, (ii) the calculations demonstrating such compliance or non-compliance, and (iii) whether any Default or Event of Default has occurred and is continuing.
**Other Affirmative Covenants:**
> \(f\) Maintenance of corporate existence, organizational structure, rights, privileges, and franchises;
>
> \(g\) Timely payment of all taxes, assessments, and governmental charges (except those being contested in good faith with adequate reserves maintained in accordance with GAAP);
>
> \(h\) Maintenance and preservation of properties, equipment, and assets in good working order and condition (ordinary wear and tear excepted), and maintenance of insurance policies in such amounts and against such risks as are customary for companies of similar size in similar industries;
>
> \(i\) Compliance in all material respects with all applicable laws, rules, and regulations, including without limitation all environmental laws and regulations applicable to the Borrower\'s environmental remediation and waste management operations;
>
> \(j\) Access and inspection rights --- the Borrower shall permit representatives of the Administrative Agent and the Lenders to visit and inspect the properties of the Borrower and its subsidiaries, examine their books and records, and discuss their affairs, finances, and condition with their officers and independent auditors, upon reasonable prior notice and during normal business hours (and without notice during the continuance of an Event of Default);
>
> \(k\) Use of proceeds consistent with the stated purposes set forth in this Term Sheet and the definitive Credit Agreement;
>
> \(l\) Additional guarantors and collateral --- the Borrower shall cause each newly formed or acquired domestic subsidiary (other than an excluded subsidiary) to become a Guarantor and to pledge its assets as Collateral within 60 days of formation or acquisition (or such longer period as may be agreed by the Administrative Agent);
>
> \(m\) ERISA compliance --- the Borrower and its ERISA Affiliates shall comply in all material respects with ERISA and the Internal Revenue Code with respect to each Plan;
>
> \(n\) Maintenance of proper books and records in accordance with GAAP;
>
> \(o\) Environmental compliance and reporting --- enhanced affirmative environmental covenants appropriate for the Borrower\'s business, including periodic environmental compliance reporting and prompt notice of any material environmental claims, liabilities, or violations; and
>
> \(p\) Post-closing obligations --- the Borrower shall complete all post-closing deliverables as set forth in a schedule to be attached as an exhibit to the Credit Agreement, with a 90-day post-closing period from the Closing Date (or such longer period as may be agreed by the Administrative Agent in its reasonable discretion).
**[Section 9 --- Negative Covenants]**
The definitive Credit Agreement shall contain negative covenants customary for transactions of this type, including without limitation the following restrictions (subject to customary exceptions and baskets to be agreed upon in the definitive Credit Agreement):
**Section 9.1 --- Indebtedness**
The Borrower and its subsidiaries shall not create, incur, assume, or suffer to exist any indebtedness, except for the following:
> \(a\) Indebtedness under the Credit Facilities;
>
> \(b\) A general indebtedness basket of \$5,000,000 (\$5.0 million) in aggregate principal amount outstanding at any time;
>
> \(c\) Capital lease obligations in an aggregate amount not to exceed \$7,500,000 (\$7.5 million) outstanding at any time;
>
> \(d\) Acquisition indebtedness incurred in connection with Permitted Acquisitions, subject to pro forma compliance with the Total Net Leverage Ratio not exceeding 4.00x after giving effect to such indebtedness;
>
> \(e\) Purchase money indebtedness in a customary basket amount (to be agreed in the definitive Credit Agreement);
>
> \(f\) Intercompany indebtedness among Loan Parties (i.e., the Borrower and its subsidiary Guarantors), subject to subordination provisions to be set forth in the definitive Credit Agreement;
>
> \(g\) Existing indebtedness as of the Closing Date, as set forth on a schedule to the Credit Agreement; and
>
> \(h\) Other customary exceptions, including refinancing indebtedness, contingent obligations permitted hereunder, and other exceptions to be agreed in the definitive Credit Agreement.
**Section 9.2 --- Liens**
The Borrower and its subsidiaries shall not create, incur, assume, or suffer to exist any lien on any of their properties or assets, except for Permitted Liens. \"Permitted Liens\" shall include customary carve-outs to be set forth in the definitive Credit Agreement, including liens securing the Credit Facilities, existing liens set forth on a schedule, purchase money liens, statutory liens (including tax, mechanics\', materialmen\'s, and carriers\' liens), judgment liens below a specified threshold, and other customary exceptions.
**Section 9.3 --- Restricted Payments**
The Borrower and its subsidiaries shall not declare, make, or pay any dividend, distribution, or other restricted payment to any equity holder, except as follows:
> \(a\) No dividends or distributions to equity holders of Cascade Holdings LLC or the Borrower shall be permitted if (x) an Event of Default exists or would result therefrom, or (y) the Borrower is not in pro forma compliance with all financial covenants set forth in Section 11 after giving effect to such dividend or distribution;
>
> \(b\) *Tax Distributions:* Tax distributions shall be permitted at all times to the extent necessary for Cascade Holdings LLC (and its direct and indirect equity holders) to pay federal, state, and local income taxes attributable to the Borrower\'s taxable income, calculated at the highest combined marginal rate applicable to any such equity holder;
>
> \(c\) *Annual Management Fee to Sponsor:* The Borrower shall be permitted to pay an annual management, monitoring, and advisory fee to Whitmore Capital Partners LLC or its affiliates in an amount not to exceed \$1,500,000 (\$1.5 million) per fiscal year. Such management fee shall be payable in arrears and shall be subject to subordination or deferral to the extent an Event of Default exists; and
>
> \(d\) Customary exceptions for repurchases of equity interests from current or former employees, officers, directors, or consultants (subject to an annual cap to be agreed in the definitive Credit Agreement).
**Section 9.4 --- Capital Expenditures**
The Borrower and its subsidiaries shall not make or commit to make capital expenditures in any fiscal year in excess of \$12,000,000 (\$12.0 million) (the \"Annual CapEx Cap\").
**Carryforward:** Unused amounts under the Annual CapEx Cap for any fiscal year may be carried forward to the immediately following fiscal year, in an amount not to exceed 25% of the unused portion of the Annual CapEx Cap for such prior fiscal year (i.e., a maximum carryforward amount of \$3,000,000 per year, calculated as \$12,000,000 multiplied by 25%). For the avoidance of doubt, carryforward amounts may not be further carried forward beyond one fiscal year --- that is, any carryforward amounts not utilized in the immediately following fiscal year shall be forfeited and shall not be available in any subsequent fiscal year (\"use it or lose it\" after one year of carryforward).
Capital expenditures funded with insurance proceeds or condemnation awards shall not count against the Annual CapEx Cap. The Annual CapEx Cap shall be prorated for any partial fiscal year (including the fiscal year in which the Closing Date occurs).
**Section 9.5 --- Permitted Acquisitions**
Acquisitions by the Borrower and its subsidiaries shall be permitted (each, a \"Permitted Acquisition\"), subject to the satisfaction of each of the following conditions:
> \(a\) The total consideration for any individual Permitted Acquisition (including the aggregate amount of all cash consideration, the face amount of all seller notes, the value of any assumed indebtedness, and the fair market value of any non-cash consideration) shall not exceed \$25,000,000 (\$25.0 million) per acquisition (the \"Individual Acquisition Cap\");
>
> \(b\) The aggregate total consideration for all Permitted Acquisitions during the term of the Credit Facilities shall not exceed \$60,000,000 (\$60.0 million) (the \"Aggregate Acquisition Cap\");
>
> \(c\) The Borrower shall be in pro forma compliance with the Total Net Leverage Ratio of not greater than 4.00x after giving effect to such Permitted Acquisition and any related indebtedness incurred in connection therewith, as demonstrated by a pro forma Compliance Certificate delivered to the Administrative Agent;
>
> \(d\) No Default or Event of Default shall exist at the time of, or would result from, such Permitted Acquisition;
>
> \(e\) The acquired entity or business (or assets) shall be in a line of business reasonably related to the Borrower\'s existing environmental remediation and waste management services business;
>
> \(f\) The acquired entity (if an entity acquisition) shall become a Guarantor under the Credit Agreement and shall pledge its assets as Collateral within 60 days of the closing of such Permitted Acquisition (or such longer period as may be agreed by the Administrative Agent); and
>
> \(g\) The Borrower shall deliver to the Administrative Agent a pro forma Compliance Certificate, together with such other financial and other information as the Administrative Agent may reasonably request, no later than 10 Business Days prior to the consummation of such Permitted Acquisition (or such shorter period as may be agreed by the Administrative Agent).
Acquisitions in which the total consideration exceeds the Individual Acquisition Cap or would cause the aggregate consideration for all acquisitions to exceed the Aggregate Acquisition Cap shall require the prior written consent of the Required Lenders.
**Section 9.6 --- Asset Sales**
The Borrower and its subsidiaries shall not sell, transfer, convey, or otherwise dispose of any assets, except as follows:
> \(a\) Permitted asset sales --- dispositions of assets in an aggregate amount not to exceed \$3,000,000 (\$3.0 million) per fiscal year for non-core asset dispositions;
>
> \(b\) Net Cash Proceeds from any individual asset sale in excess of \$1,000,000 (\$1.0 million) per transaction shall be subject to mandatory prepayment pursuant to Section 10.2 below;
>
> \(c\) Customary exceptions, including dispositions of obsolete, worn-out, or surplus equipment in the ordinary course of business, dispositions of inventory in the ordinary course of business, and other exceptions to be set forth in the definitive Credit Agreement.
**Section 9.7 --- Other Negative Covenants (Summary)**
The definitive Credit Agreement shall also include the following additional negative covenants, in each case subject to customary exceptions and carve-outs:
> \(a\) *Fundamental Changes:* Restrictions on mergers, consolidations, dissolutions, and liquidations, subject to customary exceptions (including mergers of wholly owned subsidiaries into other Loan Parties);
>
> \(b\) *Transactions with Affiliates:* Restrictions on transactions with affiliates --- all transactions with affiliates shall be on terms no less favorable to the Borrower than those that would be obtained in a comparable arm\'s length transaction with a non-affiliated person, and transactions above a specified dollar threshold (to be agreed in the definitive Credit Agreement) shall require prior approval by a majority of the disinterested members of the board of directors (or equivalent governing body) of the Borrower;
>
> \(c\) *Amendments to Material Agreements:* Restrictions on amendments or modifications to organizational documents, the Acquisition Agreement, and other material agreements, to the extent such amendments or modifications are materially adverse to the interests of the Lenders, without the prior written consent of the Administrative Agent;
>
> \(d\) *Changes in Fiscal Year:* The Borrower shall not change its fiscal year end from December 31 without the prior written consent of the Required Lenders;
>
> \(e\) *Negative Pledge and Restrictive Agreements:* Restrictions on the ability of the Borrower and its subsidiaries to enter into negative pledge clauses and other restrictive agreements that would restrict the ability of any subsidiary to make distributions to the Borrower or to grant liens in favor of the Administrative Agent, subject to customary exceptions;
>
> \(f\) *Line of Business:* The Borrower shall not materially change or alter the nature of its line of business from environmental remediation and waste management services and businesses reasonably related or ancillary thereto;
>
> \(g\) *Sale-Leaseback Transactions:* Restrictions on sale-leaseback transactions, subject to customary exceptions; and
>
> \(h\) *Swap Agreements:* Restrictions on swap and hedging agreements --- the Borrower and its subsidiaries shall only enter into swap or hedging agreements for bona fide hedging purposes and not for speculative purposes.
**[Section 10 --- Mandatory Prepayments]**
**Section 10.1 --- Excess Cash Flow Sweep**
The Borrower shall prepay the Term Loan A (and any outstanding DDTL draws) with a percentage of Excess Cash Flow for each fiscal year, calculated as follows:
**Percentage Sweep:**
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Total Net Leverage Ratio**                         **ECF Sweep Percentage**
  ---------------------------------------------------- -----------------------------------
  Greater than or equal to 4.00x                       50% of Excess Cash Flow
  Greater than or equal to 3.50x and less than 4.00x   25% of Excess Cash Flow
  Less than 3.50x                                      0% (no sweep)
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
